      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A patient with primary angina showed intermittent ST elevation (with and without chest pain), during two exercise tests performed on consecutive days; the same ST changes were also seen during the recovery phase. The electrocardiographic changes recorded in this patient may be considered an example of myocardial response to spasm-related ischemia."},
